1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:01,960
Welcome back.

2
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:05,721
The storage, the memory
and the command line are ready.

3
00:00:06,071 --> 00:00:11,982
Now we read the agent's turn line by
line, run a demo across two days, use every

4
00:00:11,982 --> 00:00:15,677
privacy feature on
purpose, and look at the tests.

5
00:00:16,027 --> 00:00:21,454
Then we wrap up the module with
interview questions, a quiz, and your extension

6
00:00:21,454 --> 00:00:22,141
challenge.

7
00:00:23,941 --> 00:00:25,569
First, the system prompt.

8
00:00:25,919 --> 00:00:32,209
As in Module 3, it explains why: the
companion remembers through long-term memory,

9
00:00:32,209 --> 00:00:35,430
because a conversation alone is forgotten.

10
00:00:36,030 --> 00:00:41,520
It says what's worth saving, one fact
per call, and to use what it remembers to

11
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:44,091
personalise explanations and quizzes.

12
00:00:44,691 --> 00:00:46,362
And never to save secrets.

13
00:00:46,712 --> 00:00:49,846
Remember, the prompt
asks, but the code enforces.

14
00:00:51,646 --> 00:00:52,837
Here's one turn.

15
00:00:53,187 --> 00:00:56,976
We remember how many messages
there were, then run the turn.

16
00:00:57,576 --> 00:01:03,826
If the turn didn't end with an answer, a
refusal, a cut off reply, too many steps,

17
00:01:03,826 --> 00:01:05,579
we remove its messages.

18
00:01:05,929 --> 00:01:07,571
Never save half a turn.

19
00:01:08,171 --> 00:01:13,731
After a good answer, compact folds old
turns into the summary, if we're over the

20
00:01:13,731 --> 00:01:14,148
limit.

21
00:01:14,498 --> 00:01:15,783
That's lesson three.

22
00:01:16,383 --> 00:01:20,218
An API error undoes the
turn too, and is reported.

23
00:01:20,818 --> 00:01:26,087
And finally, the whole session is
saved in one transaction, as in lesson five.

24
00:01:27,887 --> 00:01:33,198
Inside the turn: add the user's
message, and build the system prompt for this

25
00:01:33,198 --> 00:01:36,578
message, with the
relevant facts and the summary.

26
00:01:37,178 --> 00:01:39,075
Then the loop from Module 4.

27
00:01:39,425 --> 00:01:45,418
Each reply is stored as plain JSON
blocks, so it can be saved to the database, and

28
00:01:45,418 --> 00:01:46,879
sent again tomorrow.

29
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:50,553
No tool calls means
the model has answered.

30
00:01:51,153 --> 00:01:57,719
Otherwise, every memory tool call runs,
a refused secret becomes an error result,

31
00:01:57,719 --> 00:02:02,502
and all the results go back
in one message, as in Module 5.

32
00:02:04,302 --> 00:02:05,363
Now the demo.

33
00:02:05,713 --> 00:02:08,546
It's the next day: a
new session called tue.

34
00:02:08,896 --> 00:02:11,972
The conversation from
mon isn't sent at all.

35
00:02:12,572 --> 00:02:13,654
What's my name?

36
00:02:14,004 --> 00:02:15,524
A new, empty session.

37
00:02:15,874 --> 00:02:20,362
But the answer is Anuj, from
long-term memory in the system prompt.

38
00:02:20,962 --> 00:02:21,755
Quiz me.

39
00:02:22,105 --> 00:02:27,210
It remembered that I find recursion
hard, so the question is about recursion.

40
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:30,243
That's what memory is for: personal help.

41
00:02:30,843 --> 00:02:33,491
Now, forget that I find recursion hard.

42
00:02:33,841 --> 00:02:38,933
Two steps: recall finds the fact and
its number, then forget fact deletes it.

43
00:02:39,533 --> 00:02:40,676
And a password.

44
00:02:41,026 --> 00:02:44,303
The model tried to save
it, and our code refused.

45
00:02:44,653 --> 00:02:47,768
The error went back to
the model as an observation.

46
00:02:49,568 --> 00:02:52,532
Another user, Riya,
asks the same question.

47
00:02:52,882 --> 00:02:54,375
She doesn't get my name.

48
00:02:54,725 --> 00:02:56,837
Every query filters by user.

49
00:02:57,437 --> 00:03:00,611
Now we lower the summary
limit, to see compaction.

50
00:03:00,961 --> 00:03:04,237
The footer says: two
old messages summarized.

51
00:03:04,837 --> 00:03:06,987
History shows the session as stored.

52
00:03:07,337 --> 00:03:09,022
On top, the running summary.

53
00:03:09,372 --> 00:03:11,885
Then the recent turns, word for word.

54
00:03:12,235 --> 00:03:14,493
We show the first and last lines here.

55
00:03:15,093 --> 00:03:21,112
Sessions lists my conversations: mon and
tue, with message counts, and tue now has a

56
00:03:21,112 --> 00:03:21,685
summary.

57
00:03:22,285 --> 00:03:23,202
Retention.

58
00:03:23,552 --> 00:03:28,728
Pretend it's January: purge
deletes sessions not used for thirty days.

59
00:03:29,078 --> 00:03:31,412
Both are gone, with their messages.

60
00:03:32,012 --> 00:03:37,695
And delete me asks first, then deletes
every fact and session of mine, and nobody

61
00:03:37,695 --> 00:03:38,186
else's.

62
00:03:39,986 --> 00:03:46,165
The tests run the real agent, tools and
SQLite against the fake model, with a new

63
00:03:46,165 --> 00:03:48,759
temporary database for every test.

64
00:03:49,109 --> 00:03:54,797
This one proves the point of lesson one:
in another session, without the history or

65
00:03:54,797 --> 00:03:57,401
a saved fact, the name can't be known.

66
00:03:58,001 --> 00:04:03,920
And this one proves long-term memory: a
new session starts with no messages, still

67
00:04:03,920 --> 00:04:09,333
answers Anuj, and the request really
carried the fact in its system prompt.

68
00:04:11,133 --> 00:04:16,809
Forty-one tests: memory, the database,
the conversation, the tools, the agent and

69
00:04:16,809 --> 00:04:18,001
the command line.

70
00:04:18,351 --> 00:04:21,046
All passing, with no key and no network.

71
00:04:21,646 --> 00:04:25,330
And mypy, in strict
mode, is happy with every type.

72
00:04:27,130 --> 00:04:28,358
Common problems.

73
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:34,259
It forgets in the middle of a chat: a
message or reply isn't appended to the history

74
00:04:34,259 --> 00:04:34,854
you send.

75
00:04:35,454 --> 00:04:40,976
A four hundred error about a tool result
without a tool use: you trimmed between a

76
00:04:40,976 --> 00:04:41,313
pair.

77
00:04:41,663 --> 00:04:43,459
Cut only where a turn starts.

78
00:04:44,059 --> 00:04:48,515
Another user's facts appear: a
query is missing the user filter.

79
00:04:48,865 --> 00:04:50,636
Write a test for isolation.

80
00:04:51,236 --> 00:04:54,886
And database is locked:
two programs writing at once.

81
00:04:55,236 --> 00:04:59,455
Keep transactions short, or
move to PostgreSQL for many writers.

82
00:05:01,255 --> 00:05:02,396
Interview corner.

83
00:05:02,746 --> 00:05:07,440
Design memory for a tutoring
agent used by thousands of students.

84
00:05:10,040 --> 00:05:13,884
A good answer: one set of
rows per student, in PostgreSQL.

85
00:05:14,234 --> 00:05:18,498
For each session, a window of
recent turns and a running summary.

86
00:05:18,848 --> 00:05:24,251
Long-term facts saved with tools, and
the relevant ones put in the system prompt.

87
00:05:24,601 --> 00:05:30,878
Secrets refused in code, a retention
rule, a delete my data command, and tests for

88
00:05:30,878 --> 00:05:31,643
isolation.

89
00:05:31,993 --> 00:05:35,304
And at scale,
embeddings to find relevant facts.

90
00:05:35,654 --> 00:05:41,329
The trap: one giant shared history,
or letting the model choose the user ID.

91
00:05:41,929 --> 00:05:42,865
Follow-up.

92
00:05:43,215 --> 00:05:45,760
A user asks you to delete their data.

93
00:05:46,110 --> 00:05:47,253
What must happen?

94
00:05:49,853 --> 00:05:55,171
Delete their facts, their sessions and
their messages, and backups and logs too,

95
00:05:55,171 --> 00:05:56,832
according to your policy.

96
00:05:57,182 --> 00:05:59,921
Confirm it, and make
sure nothing loads it again.

97
00:06:00,271 --> 00:06:05,524
In code, that's one transaction
filtered by the user, with cascades for the

98
00:06:05,524 --> 00:06:06,995
messages, and a test.

99
00:06:07,345 --> 00:06:11,933
The trap is deleting the facts, but
forgetting the stored conversations.

100
00:06:13,733 --> 00:06:15,616
Let's recap the whole module.

101
00:06:15,966 --> 00:06:17,617
The API is stateless.

102
00:06:17,967 --> 00:06:20,456
All memory is data your code sends.

103
00:06:21,056 --> 00:06:26,165
Short-term memory is a window of
recent turns, cut where a turn starts.

104
00:06:26,765 --> 00:06:30,738
Summary memory folds old
turns into a running summary.

105
00:06:31,338 --> 00:06:36,984
Long-term memory is facts saved with
tools, with the relevant ones in the system

106
00:06:36,984 --> 00:06:37,478
prompt.

107
00:06:38,078 --> 00:06:44,278
And SQLite stores it all, with
parameters, transactions, a user ID on every row,

108
00:06:44,278 --> 00:06:46,138
retention, and deletion.

109
00:06:47,938 --> 00:06:49,834
Module quiz, question one.

110
00:06:50,184 --> 00:06:54,472
Why does a chatbot remember
earlier messages in a conversation?

111
00:07:00,672 --> 00:07:04,253
Because your code resends
the history with each request.

112
00:07:04,603 --> 00:07:06,635
The API itself is stateless.

113
00:07:08,435 --> 00:07:09,525
Question two.

114
00:07:09,875 --> 00:07:12,755
Where must a sliding
window cut the conversation?

115
00:07:18,955 --> 00:07:22,540
Where a turn starts: a
user message with plain text.

116
00:07:22,890 --> 00:07:24,635
That keeps tool pairs together.

117
00:07:26,435 --> 00:07:27,566
Question three.

118
00:07:27,916 --> 00:07:30,433
What's the main
trade-off of summary memory?

119
00:07:36,633 --> 00:07:40,189
Details can be lost,
and it costs an extra call.

120
00:07:41,989 --> 00:07:43,103
Question four.

121
00:07:43,453 --> 00:07:47,001
The model calls remember
fact with a user's password.

122
00:07:47,351 --> 00:07:48,416
What should happen?

123
00:07:54,616 --> 00:07:57,915
Your code refuses it,
and returns a tool error.

124
00:07:58,265 --> 00:08:00,449
Prompts guide, code enforces.

125
00:08:02,249 --> 00:08:03,613
And question five.

126
00:08:03,963 --> 00:08:07,210
Which of these queries
is safe from SQL injection?

127
00:08:13,410 --> 00:08:14,018
B.

128
00:08:14,368 --> 00:08:17,809
It's the only one that
passes the value as a parameter.

129
00:08:18,159 --> 00:08:20,728
The others paste it into the SQL text.

130
00:08:22,528 --> 00:08:24,935
Now some practice, from easy to hard.

131
00:08:25,285 --> 00:08:26,631
Pause and try them.

132
00:08:26,981 --> 00:08:30,544
The answers are in the
module's quiz dot md file.

133
00:08:31,144 --> 00:08:31,782
One.

134
00:08:32,132 --> 00:08:37,593
Write a window by tokens function,
which keeps recent turns up to a token budget.

135
00:08:38,193 --> 00:08:38,815
Two.

136
00:08:39,165 --> 00:08:43,254
From: I'm Sam, I'm tired
today, I passed my Python exam.

137
00:08:43,604 --> 00:08:45,264
Which facts should be saved?

138
00:08:45,864 --> 00:08:46,561
Three.

139
00:08:46,911 --> 00:08:49,991
Write the SQL to
count each user's messages.

140
00:08:50,591 --> 00:08:52,244
And four, a scenario.

141
00:08:52,594 --> 00:08:55,459
A customer support
bot remembers customers.

142
00:08:55,809 --> 00:08:58,864
Design its memory, and its privacy rules.

143
00:09:06,664 --> 00:09:08,271
Your extension challenge.

144
00:09:08,621 --> 00:09:13,302
Pick one or more, and write a
test for each, using the fake API.

145
00:09:13,902 --> 00:09:19,525
Add export and import commands, that
save and load your data as a JSON file.

146
00:09:20,125 --> 00:09:25,313
Make some facts expire, for example
struggle facts older than sixty days.

147
00:09:25,913 --> 00:09:29,214
Size the window by
tokens, instead of turns.

148
00:09:29,814 --> 00:09:35,560
Or swap SQLite for PostgreSQL, with
psycopg, and keep the same tests passing.

149
00:09:37,360 --> 00:09:42,562
These are the official documentation
pages for this module, including Claude's

150
00:09:42,562 --> 00:09:46,963
ready-made memory tool, which
you can compare with what you built.

151
00:09:47,313 --> 00:09:51,920
Links are in the description, with the
full source code and the question bank.

152
00:09:58,520 --> 00:10:00,351
That's Module 6 complete.

153
00:10:00,701 --> 00:10:06,537
Your agent now remembers: within a chat,
across days, and only what it should, with

154
00:10:06,537 --> 00:10:08,577
every user's data kept apart.

155
00:10:08,927 --> 00:10:14,913
In Module 7, we make agents reliable and
efficient: retries, caching, budgets, and

156
00:10:14,913 --> 00:10:16,447
tracing what they do.

157
00:10:16,796 --> 00:10:17,739
See you there.
